  "question": {
    "text": "Let $P$ and $Q$ be $3 \\times 3$ matrices with $P \\neq Q$. If $P^3=Q^3$ and $P^2 Q=Q^2 P$, then determinant of $\\left(P^2+Q^2\\right)$ is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$-2$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$1$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$0$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-1$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$P^3=Q^3$\n$P^3-P^2 Q=Q^3-Q^2 P$\n$P^2(P-Q)=Q^2(Q-P)$\n$P^2(P-Q)+Q^2(P-Q)=O$\n$\\left(P^2+Q^2\\right)(P-Q)=O \\quad \\Rightarrow\\left|P^2+Q^2\\right|=0$"
  }
}